# Time System

The Time System governs the flow of the game world, controlling how player actions consume time and how each day progresses.
Time is a limited resource and serves as a core source of pressure, forcing the player to make decisions about how to spend each day.

---

##  Core Concept

Time continuously advances as the player performs actions.

Every major activity consumes time, limiting how much the player can accomplish in a single day.

The player must balance time between:

- Working to earn money  
- Caring for Grandpa  
- Managing personal wellbeing  
- Exploring the city  

---

##  Time Structure

The game operates on a daily cycle:

- Each day has a set start time  
- Time progresses in hours and minutes  
- The day ends when the player chooses to sleep  

### Example:
- Morning → Work / Planning  
- Afternoon → Activities / Travel  
- Evening → Care / Recovery  

---

##  Time Advancement

Time advances through both player actions and real-time progression.

### Actions that advance time:

-  Working (4 / 8 / 12 hours)
-  Sitting with Grandpa  
-  Working out  
-  Shopping
-  Cooking (planned)

Each action advances time by a defined amount.

---

##  Day Transition

The player ends the day by sleeping.

### On Sleep:
- Time resets to the next day  
- Daily limits are reset (e.g. medicine usage)  
- Systems update:
  - Grandpa condition  
  - Player stats  
  - City state  

---

##  Time as a Resource

Time acts as a constraint that limits player behavior.

Spending time in one area reduces the ability to act in others.

### Example Trade-Offs:

- Working longer → less time for Grandpa  
- Caring for Grandpa → less time to earn money  
- Exploring → risk of running out of time for responsibilities  

---

##  System Interactions

The Time System directly affects all major gameplay systems:

-  Job System → consumes large amounts of time  
-  Grandpa System → requires time investment  
-  Player Stats → activities affect stress, morale, stamina  
-  Shop System → requires travel and time  
-  City System → events may occur at specific times  

---

##  Future Expansion (Planned)

### Timed Events
- Certain events occur only at specific times:
  - Protests  
  - Store hours  
  - NPC schedules  

### Time-Based Restrictions
- Some locations or activities may be unavailable depending on time of day  

### Consequences of Poor Time Management
- Missing work shifts  
- Inability to care for Grandpa  
- Increased stress from poor planning  

---

##  Design Purpose

The Time System is designed to:

- Create constant pressure  
- Force prioritization and planning  
- Limit player actions in a meaningful way  
- Reinforce the daily survival loop  

---

##  Example Scenario

The player chooses to:

- Work an 8-hour shift → time advances significantly  
- Return home late → limited time to care for Grandpa  
- Skip rest → increased stress the next day  

This creates a chain of consequences driven entirely by time management.
